# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.hypothesis/
*.egg-info/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/

# Environment
.env

# Claude
.claude/settings.local.json
# Native parallel-session worktrees live in-repo here (ADR-61/#107); ignore so they don't
# show as untracked AND so gitignore-respecting walkers (ruff) don't descend into the full
# checkout. pytest is already safe via its default `.*` norecursedirs (dot-dir skip).
.claude/worktrees/

# Session-end closure proposals (ADR-70 Tier-1; ephemeral, reviewed at next /boot —
# the durable record is the eventual `closes [#N]` commit + JOURNAL, ADR-65)
logs/PROPOSALS-*.md

# Fleet-health digest (ADR-80 mutable — auto-refreshed by fleet_health.py, never committed;
# durable Tier-2 audit record is docs/audits/*.md, committed by audit.py per ADR-80 §3)
logs/FLEET-HEALTH.md

# Enforcement-coverage digest (Informant Organ, Stage-2 enforcement-transfer — read-only
# reporter, auto-refreshed by scripts/enforcement_coverage.py; never committed, same ephemeral
# pattern as FLEET-HEALTH.md. Writing it must never dirty the tree / trip session-end backpressure.)
logs/ENFORCEMENT-COVERAGE.md

# Lived-workflow sandbox operator funnel (Slice A: isolation-proof outcomes; read-only reporter,
# same ephemeral pattern as ENFORCEMENT-COVERAGE — the sandbox writes it, it is never committed).
logs/LIVED-WORKFLOW.md

# Fleet CLAUDE.md boundary-marker drift digest (#312 read-only reporter; auto-refreshed by
# scripts/boundary_report.py, never committed — same ephemeral pattern as FLEET-HEALTH.md.)
logs/BOUNDARY-DRIFT.md

# L5a descriptive analytics digest — hotspot / change-coupling / rot frames ([#384] read-only
# reporter; auto-refreshed by scripts/fleet_analytics.py, never committed — same ephemeral
# pattern as FLEET-HEALTH.md. Frames change on every commit by construction, so committing
# this would churn the tree constantly and trip session-end backpressure.)
logs/FLEET-ANALYTICS.md

# Fleet-parity digest + checker-run JSONL events (#328 read-only checker, WARN-only v1 —
# scripts/fleet_parity.py; same ephemeral pattern as ENFORCEMENT-COVERAGE. The events file
# is append-only, rotation-capped (single .1 backup), gitignored runtime per FR-8/FR-13;
# the durable record is the JOURNAL-pasted verdict table + eventual committed digests.)
logs/FLEET-PARITY.md
logs/parity-events.jsonl
logs/parity-events.jsonl.1

# Ecosystem mutable pointers (ADR-80 mutable/durable split — high-churn pointer, not committed;
# durable records are ecosystem/*/history/*.md + docs/audits/*.md, committed by audit.py)
ecosystem/*/state.yaml

# Session-end gate override (ADR-85) — ephemeral local signal + audit log, never committed.
# The token is a HEAD-bound one-shot the Stop-hook pure-reads; OVERRIDES.md is the local
# override-rate audit trail (matches the logs/PROPOSALS-* / FLEET-HEALTH ephemeral pattern).
logs/.session-override-token
logs/OVERRIDES.md

# Coherence forgotten-version-bump nudge log (CLAUDE.md §9 — non-blocking hook that always
# exits 0; this is its ephemeral append-only record, never committed; same ephemeral pattern
# as logs/PROPOSALS-* / FLEET-HEALTH / OVERRIDES). The durable signal is the reconciled_versions
# audit check + the eventual version bump in git history.
logs/coherence-nudge.log

# Vendored Pyright langserver for the reverse-dep oracle (#193, ADR-89). The version is
# pinned in package.json + package-lock.json (committed); the heavy node_modules tree is
# rebuilt per-checkout via `npm install` (bootstrap documented in scripts/reverse_dep_oracle.py).
node_modules/

# OS
*.tmp
*.bak

# Personal scratch / temp work (unrelated to repo content)
temp/
